    summary: "D07001 is an oral softgel capsule form of the chemotherapy gemcitabine developed by InnoPharmax: the ClinicalTrials.gov record of NCT06622057 states that the 'D07001-softgel capsule is an oral gemcitabine'. ClinicalTrials.gov describes the intervention as: D07001-softgel capsules: 3 times per week (on Days 1, 3, 5, 8, 10, 12, 15, 17, and 19 of a 21-day cycle, 9 doses per cycle). Xeloda (or TS-1): twice daily for 14 consecutive days followed by 7 days rest (1 treatment cycle). It has two registered trials at phase 2 or above in biliary tract cancer (registry read 18 November 2026): the phase 2/3 study NCT05065957 (Study of Combination Therapy of D07001-Softgel Capsules and Xeloda/TS-1 in Subjects With Advanced Biliary Tract Cancer), which was terminated after 19 participants because, in the sponsor's words, the 'Dose-finding stage has been completed, and dose-expanding stage was not conducted due to design amendment', and the recruiting phase 3 study NCT06622057 (D07001 Softgel-Capsules and Capecitabine Combination Therapy in Patients With Advanced Biliary Tract Cancer), which compares it with placebo, each given with capecitabine. The largest, NCT06622057, plans to enrol 240 participants with primary completion expected 2028-12-31. Status reflects the highest phase registered on ClinicalTrials.gov; no efficacy results are recorded here.",
    targets: [], cancers: ["cholangiocarcinoma"], companies: ["innopharmax"], trials: ["nct05065957", "nct06622057"],
