    summary: "TBI-1301 (mipetresgene autoleucel, mip-cel) is a cell therapy developed by Takara Bio. The company's earlier registry record names it as NY-ESO-1 T cell receptor gene transduced autologous T lymphocytes (NCT03250325, a phase 1/2 study in synovial sarcoma that enrolled 8 people and is completed, with no results posted on the registry). ClinicalTrials.gov describes the intervention as: Split dose of TBI-1301 is administered intravenously for 2 days following cyclophosphamide/fludarabine pre-treatment. The current study, NCT07174427 (Multi-centre Study of TBI-1301 (INN: Mipetresgene Autoleucel; Mip-cel) in Patients With NY-ESO-1 Positive Synovial Sarcoma), is registered as phase 3, was recruiting when read on 18 November 2026, and plans to enrol 5 participants with primary completion expected 2032-03. An investigator-led phase 1 study in solid tumours in Toronto (NCT02869217) is also registered. Status reflects the highest phase registered on ClinicalTrials.gov; no efficacy results are recorded here.",
