    summary: "TNG462, now named vopimetostat on the registry, is a small-molecule drug developed by Tango Therapeutics; Servier Bio-Innovation sponsors one trial that combines it with Servier's own drug S095035. Its target is PRMT5 (MTAP-deleted cancers) (the sponsor names PRMT5). The sponsor states: A selective PRMT5 inhibitor administered orally, developed for tumours with an MTAP homozygous deletion. ClinicalTrials.gov describes the intervention as: TNG462, a selective PRMT5 inhibitor, will be administered orally. On the registry on 18 November 2026 it was in three industry-led phase 1/2 trials, none of them phase 3: NCT05732831 in MTAP-deleted solid tumours (recruiting; 225 participants planned, primary completion expected 2027-06), NCT06922591 with RAS inhibitors or chemotherapy in pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma and non-small-cell lung cancer (recruiting), and Servier's NCT06188702 (no longer recruiting). A fourth phase 1/2 study, NCT07897734, with ERAS-0015, had not started recruiting. Status reflects the highest phase registered on ClinicalTrials.gov; no efficacy results are recorded here.",
